# E2E Testing Rules (Playwright)

## Two suites, two owners — do not blur the line
- `tests/e2e/ui/**` — browser-driven, Playwright `page` fixture, one spec per MFE's critical
  journey plus one cross-MFE journey through the dashboard host. This is the only layer that
  can catch Module Federation runtime issues; do not use it to assert backend state directly.
- `tests/e2e/api/**` — Playwright `request` context only, no browser. If a spec here does not
  need a page, do not give it one — the whole point is avoiding browser startup cost.
- `tests/e2e/fixtures/**` is joint-owned by both suites. Check it does not already have what
  you need before adding a duplicate.

## Auth and test data
- Log in once via `fixtures/auth.ts`, reuse `storageState` across specs — do not log in
  through the UI in every test.
- Each spec (or `test.describe` block) creates its own project/user via the API and cleans it
  up afterward. Never assume shared state, and never depend on the specific rows seeded by
  `R__01_seed_local_dev.sql` — that seed is for manual local dev, not automated isolation.
- Use `fixtures/ids.ts` for collision-safe naming so parallel workers never collide on a
  project slug or similar unique field.

## Selectors and assertions
- Query by role/label/text (`getByRole`, `getByLabel`) the same way `.cursor/rules/frontend-testing.mdc`
  requires for Vitest — not brittle CSS classes or XPath. `data-testid` only when no accessible
  query exists.
- Assert user-visible or API-contract behavior, not internal state. A refactor that does not
  change behavior should not break the spec.
- No `waitForTimeout`/hardcoded sleeps. Wait on a real condition — element state, a specific
  response, a URL change.

## Auth/security-related specs
- Anything touching login, JWT cookies, or API keys must reflect `.cursor/rules/security.mdc`:
  httpOnly cookie behavior (never asserting a token is readable from `document.cookie` in JS),
  API keys shown once and stored hashed, and the ReDoS length/complexity guard on
  guardrail regex input actually rejecting the pattern, not just timing out.
- Assert the gateway does not expose `/internal/**` endpoints externally once those exist
  (Phase 4+, `docs/MICROSERVICES_PLAN.md` §3.2/§3.3) — this is a standing regression test,
  not a one-time manual check.

## Never
- Never let a spec or its fixtures call a real LLM provider (Anthropic/OpenAI/Azure) —
  mock/stub at the provider boundary, same rule as backend unit tests already follow.
- Never skip, `.only()`, or mark a spec `fixme` to get a run green without flagging it to the
  other SDET first.
- Never accept a generated spec as done without actually running it and reviewing the output.

## Tagging and CI
- Tag every spec `@smoke` (fast, safe for PR-path-triggered CI) or `@regression` (full suite,
  nightly only) — see `docs/TEST_PLAN.md` §7/§12 for the exact trigger conditions.
- `retries: 2` on CI, `0` locally; `trace: 'on-first-retry'`. A spec that only passes on retry
  locally is a bug in the spec, not a CI flakiness problem to paper over.
